    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"weight\" is the only thing that feels real anymore. even when i'm home, i can still smell the hospital. it's like there's no point in the rest or the sleep... everything just feels so heavy and futile. like i'm just waiting for the next disaster so i can fail at stopping it. does it ever actually get better? or is it just a cycle of being tired until you can't be anymore?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
